### Library Management System - example API requests
### Open in VS Code (REST Client extension) or JetBrains IDEs and click "Send Request".
### Start the server first:  python -m library.api

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5000

### 1. List all books  -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/books

### 2. Search books by text and/or genre  -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?q=clean&genre=Technology

### 3. Add a book  -> 201 (409 if the ISBN already exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "978-0-13-235088-4",
  "title": "Clean Code",
  "author": "Robert C. Martin",
  "genre": "Technology",
  "copies": 2
}

### 4. Add a book with an invalid ISBN  -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "978-0-13-235088-5",
  "title": "Broken ISBN",
  "author": "Nobody",
  "genre": "Fiction"
}

### 5. Register a student  -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_id": "S100",
  "name": "Asha Kumar",
  "email": "asha.kumar@example.com",
  "member_type": "student"
}

### 6. Register a member with an invalid email  -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_id": "S101",
  "name": "Bad Email",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "member_type": "student"
}

### 7. Borrow a book  -> 201 (creates a loan)
POST {{baseUrl}}/borrow
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_id": "S100",
  "isbn": "9780132350884"
}

### 8. Borrow with an unknown member  -> 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/borrow
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_id": "NOBODY",
  "isbn": "9780132350884"
}

### 9. Member details, current loans and fines  -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/members/S100

### 10. Return a book  -> 200 (response includes the fine)
POST {{baseUrl}}/return
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_id": "S100",
  "isbn": "9780132350884"
}

### 11. Return a book that is not on loan  -> 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/return
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "member_id": "S100",
  "isbn": "9780132350884"
}

### 12. Unknown member  -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/members/NOBODY
